}\\,\\text{d}x & =12{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2}\\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =12\\,\\text{arcsec}\\,u\\,{|}_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2} \\\\  & =12(\\text{arcsec}(2)-\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{2})) \\\\  & =12(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291581 13194139534487 true] [17592186291580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291582 13194139534487 true] [17592186291580 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534487 true] [17592186291580 1041 "field-1" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291580 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291581 13194139534487 true] [17592186291580 1110 #uuid "aa43e869-ffd8-534e-bab9-31a347265593" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291581 1034 "\\pi" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291581 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534487 true] [17592186291581 1111 #uuid "4c1ba5e8-56a7-56c6-a719-0e74f223e78a" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291582 1034 "2\\pi" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291582 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534487 true] [17592186291582 1111 #uuid "d66372c1-338b-5f5d-91ca-97a24d50562a" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291583 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291584 13194139534487 true] [17592186291583 1089 "q-348553" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291583 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534487 true] [17592186291583 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-3}^{\\sqrt{3}-3}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+6x+10}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291583 1113 #uuid "e8bcf7d0-5de5-553f-a324-8d00997d674e" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291583 1145 "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+6x+10 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+({3}^{2}-{3}^{2})+10 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2})-9+10 \\\\  & =(x+3)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+6x+10}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{6}{(x+3)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x+3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x+3).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x+3.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $\\sqrt{3}-3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{\\sqrt{3}-3}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+6x+10}\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0) \\\\  & =2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291584 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291585 13194139534487 true] [17592186291584 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534487 true] [17592186291584 1041 "field-1" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291584 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291585 13194139534487 true] [17592186291584 1110 #uuid "6bcb229c-b6e9-5f9a-ad69-0deda754e10f" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291585 1034 "2\\pi" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291585 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534487 true] [17592186291585 1111 #uuid "042725ef-c815-51c0-bee5-0d7e7a31f3b1" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291586 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291587 13194139534487 true] [17592186291586 1089 "q-49934" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291586 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534487 true] [17592186291586 1100 "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-3{x}^{2}-18x+6}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291586 1113 #uuid "05179cbf-a52b-578c-91d6-1ae5539de82e" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291586 1145 "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}^{2}-18x+6 & =-3({x}^{2}+6x-2) \\\\  & =-3({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+[{3}^{2}-{3}^{2}]-2) \\\\  & =-3({(x+3)}^{2}-11) \\\\  & =3(11-{(x+3)}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-3{x}^{2}-18x+6}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3(11-{(x+3)}^{2})}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33(1-(x+3)^{2}/11)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-(x+3)^{2}/11}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x+3)/\\sqrt{11})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{x+3}{\\sqrt{11}}).$  \n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{x+3}{\\sqrt{11}}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{11}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{11}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-3{x}^{2}-18x+6}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x+3)/\\sqrt{11})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\sqrt{11}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{\\sqrt{11}})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534487 true] [17592186291587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291588 13194139534487 true] [17592186291587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291589 13194139534487 true] [17592186291587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291590 13194139534487 true] [17592186291587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291591 13194139534487 true] [17592186291587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291592 13194139534